@baseUrl = http://localhost:5288

# The import and customer requests need a signed-in session and, to change anything,
# an antiforgery token. Run A, paste its token below, run B, then run A again and
# paste the new token, because a token belongs to the user who requested it.
@csrfToken = paste-token-here
@email = paste-email-here
@password = paste-password-here

### A. Get an antiforgery token, which also stores its cookie
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/antiforgery

### B. Sign in. Expect a 302 and a cookie, which your client must keep and send.
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

email={{email}}&password={{password}}

### C. Sign out
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

# Run request 1 first, then set this to the id it returns.
@batchId = 1

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health/ready

### Liveness: the app process answers, without touching SQL Server
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health/live
Accept: application/json

### 1. Upload: expect 202 with batchId and statusUrl. Poll request 3 until job.stage is Completed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/imports
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=DataBridgeBoundary

--DataBridgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="customers-sample.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./customers-sample.csv
--DataBridgeBoundary--

### 1b. Upload the same data as an Excel workbook: expect 202, then 4 rows, numbered like request 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/imports
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=DataBridgeBoundary

--DataBridgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="customers-sample.xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< ./customers-sample.xlsx
--DataBridgeBoundary--

### 2. List batches: expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/imports?page=1&pageSize=25

### 3. Progress and batch details: expect 200.
# job.stage is Queued, Parsing, Saving, Validating, Completed or Failed.
# job.processedRows, job.totalRows and job.error appear when known.
# Header positions start at 0.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}

### 4. Save the mapping using zero-based column positions: expect 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/mapping
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameColumn": 0,
  "companyColumn": 1,
  "emailColumn": 2,
  "phoneColumn": 3,
  "locationColumn": 4,
  "statusColumn": 5,
  "notesColumn": 6
}

### 5. Mapped preview, first page: expect 200 with source rows 2 and 4
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows?page=1&pageSize=2

### 6. Mapped preview, second page: expect 200 with source rows 5 and 6
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows?page=2&pageSize=2

### 7. Unknown batch: expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/999999

### 8. Invalid mapping, emailColumn is missing: expect 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/mapping
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameColumn": 0,
  "statusColumn": 5
}

### 9. Invalid mapping, the file has no column 99: expect 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/mapping
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameColumn": 99,
  "emailColumn": 2,
  "statusColumn": 5
}

### 10. Invalid paging, pageSize is over 100: expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows?page=1&pageSize=101

### 11. Queue validation: expect 202. Poll request 3 until status is ReadyForReview.
# Running it again replaces the old issues. A batch with no mapping returns 400.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/validate
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### 12. Validate an unknown batch: expect 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/999999/validate
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

# The review requests below use values from the row preview in request 5.
@rowId = 1
@customerVersion = AAAAAAAAB9E=

### 13. Correct a row. This replaces all seven drafts: expect 200 with the row revalidated
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows/{{rowId}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "draftName": "Ana Ruiz",
  "draftCompany": "Northwind",
  "draftEmail": "ana@example.com",
  "draftPhone": "555-0101",
  "draftLocation": "Queens",
  "draftStatus": "Active",
  "draftNotes": "Prefers email, not phone"
}

### 14. Approve a New row for insert: expect 200, or 409 if the row has changed.
# rowVersion comes from the row preview.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows/{{rowId}}/decision
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "Approved",
  "rowVersion": "{{rowVersion}}"
}

### 14b. Approve selected New rows together: expect 200, or 409 with nothing approved
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows/bulk-approve
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rows": [
    { "rowId": {{rowId}}, "rowVersion": "{{rowVersion}}" }
  ]
}

### 15. Approve a Conflict as an update: expect 200, or 409 if the row or customer has changed
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows/{{rowId}}/decision
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "Approved",
  "confirmUpdate": true,
  "rowVersion": "{{rowVersion}}",
  "customerVersion": "{{customerVersion}}"
}

### 16. Reject a row with a reason: expect 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/rows/{{rowId}}/decision
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "Rejected",
  "reason": "Already in the customer list"
}

### 17. Commit once every row has a decision: expect 200 with the summary, even if every row was rejected.
# Repeating it returns the same summary. Stale approvals return 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/commit
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### 18. Review and commit history: expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/imports/{{batchId}}/audit?page=1&pageSize=100

### 19. Committed customers, filtered: expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers?page=1&pageSize=25&location=Queens&status=Active

### 20. Unknown status filter: expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers?status=Archived

### 21. AI search: expect 200, outcome Applied, and the filters it used.
# Needs a signed-in user and the OpenAI:ApiKey user secret. Without the key, expect 503.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/search/ai
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Show me active customers in Queens"
}

### 22. AI search with an unsupported request: expect 200, outcome Unsupported, and no changes
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/search/ai
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Delete all customers"
}
